From 0f44c1aefd04a8629bf4cf65ff190f8140e37834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:24:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] wwphys (physics, collision, visibility, pathfinding)
 compiles; loop variables keep old MSVC's semantics

- all 93 files of wwphys compile; Umbra (third-party visibility) is switched off in the source
  (UMBRASUPPORT 0) and the level-editor-only files aren't in the build
- usual fixes: extra qualification, loop scoping, const strrchr, a nested class's name made public
  for its pool definition, projector macro no longer pastes a name onto '.'
- loop variables: where a declaration was moved above its loop (old MSVC kept it alive for the
  function), later loops at the same level now reuse it instead of declaring a new one that would
  hide it, matching old MSVC's single variable (11 loops, one in ww3d2/dx8wrapper.cpp); duplicate
  moved declarations removed
---
 ww3d2/dx8wrapper.cpp                   |  2 +-
 wwlib/binheap.h                        |  3 ++-
 wwphys/Path.cpp                        |  3 ++-
 wwphys/Pathfind.cpp                    |  9 ++++++---
